{
  "title": "Remaining small iOS parity gaps: meal plan editing, advanced photo \
filters",
  "description": "Smaller iOS gaps vs web, fine to do together or split:\n\
\n\
1. Meal plan entries can't be edited on iOS — only created/deleted \
(MealPlanView.swift, AddToMealPlanSheet.swift). Web supports editing entries \
(updateMealPlan). Add edit support (change date/meal type/notes).\n\
\n\
2. Advanced photo filters missing on iOS — web's cookbook supports filtering \
by photo file size and dimensions thresholds \
(ramekin-ui/src/pages/CookbookPage.tsx); iOS RecipeAdvancedFiltersSheet.swift \
only has has/no-photo. Add the size/dimension filters to the iOS filter \
sheet.\n\
\n\
Note: iOS meal plan calls currently go through the hand-written \
Shared/RamekinAPI.swift rather than the generated client — if \
p3-ios-replace-handwritten-api-client lands first, build on the generated \
client.",
